From: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: set_monitor_channel takes a net_device from 6.12.101

Upstream 9c4f83092775 ("wifi: cfg80211: pass net_device to
.set_monitor_channel") landed in 6.13 and was backported to 6.12.101 as a
Stable-dep-of the pmsr_free_wk deadlock fix, so gating the new signature
on 6.13 fails to build against 6.12.101+ with -Wincompatible-pointer-types.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
--- a/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -4418,7 +4418,7 @@
 }
 
 static int cfg80211_rtw_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy
-#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0))
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 101))
 	, struct net_device *dev
 	, struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef
 #elif (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 8, 0))
